From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Hunter B Hough <git@hough.ink>
Date: Sun, 16 Aug 2026 22:19:20 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 43/64] fix(github-pr-review): teach finalize how to record an
 aborted run (gcp-m7dn)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Moving finalize onto the scope body means it now runs on a path it was never
written for. Before the abort_scope wiring, finalize could only be reached
through a completed post-comment, so its instruction to record "rendered comment
path, GitHub comment id/url, mapped outcome" always had values to read. On an
aborted run those fields are legitimately absent — nothing was rendered, nothing
was posted, no verdict was mapped — and prose that lists them unconditionally
invites the same failure this branch exists to close: an operator facing an
unsatisfiable instruction either blocks or fabricates a value that makes the
record look complete.

Name the abort path explicitly, tell finalize to record the absent fields as
absent along with gc.github.review_child_outcome and the diagnostics the scope
body propagated, and forbid backfilling or carrying a value forward from an
earlier head SHA.

Also pin its close semantics, which are non-obvious: finalize closes
gc.outcome=pass on an aborted run, because its own job — writing the record —
succeeded. The failed scope member is what makes the workflow root resolve to
fail (resolveFinalizeOutcome aggregates the finalizer's blockers, and
review-scope is one of them). finalize closing fail would be reserved for a
record it genuinely could not write.

Extends the scope-wiring test with the finalize abort-path assertions.
---
 .../assets/workflows/github-pr-review/finalize.md | 15 +++++++++++++++
 gascity/tests/test_formula_assets.py              |  7 +++++++
 2 files changed, 22 insertions(+)

diff --git a/gascity/assets/workflows/github-pr-review/finalize.md b/gascity/assets/workflows/github-pr-review/finalize.md
index 4a202c5..5624e61 100644
--- a/gascity/assets/workflows/github-pr-review/finalize.md
+++ b/gascity/assets/workflows/github-pr-review/finalize.md
@@ -4,3 +4,18 @@ id, head SHA, review subject path, review report path, rendered comment path,
 GitHub comment id/url, mapped outcome, launch input URL {{github_pr_url}},
 artifact root {{artifact_root}}, context path {{context_path}}, post mode
 {{post_mode}}, and whether this run reused prior head-SHA output.
+
+This step hangs off the `review-scope` body, not off `post-comment`, so it also
+runs when the scope ABORTED — a review workflow that did not succeed, or a human
+gate that rejected the comment. On that path the fields above are legitimately
+absent: there is no rendered comment, no GitHub comment id, and no mapped
+outcome, because nothing was posted. Record them as absent and record why,
+reading `gc.github.review_child_outcome` and the scope body's propagated
+diagnostics. Do NOT invent, backfill, or carry forward a value from an earlier
+head SHA to make the record look complete — the whole point of the abort is that
+this run produced no verdict.
+
+Close this step `gc.outcome=pass` whenever it successfully recorded the result,
+including for an aborted run: this step's own job is to write the record, and
+the failed scope member is what makes the workflow root resolve to fail. Close
+`gc.outcome=fail` only when the record itself could not be written.
diff --git a/gascity/tests/test_formula_assets.py b/gascity/tests/test_formula_assets.py
index 6b813e9..b966d43 100755
--- a/gascity/tests/test_formula_assets.py
+++ b/gascity/tests/test_formula_assets.py
@@ -3680,6 +3680,13 @@ class FormulaAssetTests(unittest.TestCase):
         self.assertEqual(steps["finalize"]["needs"], ["review-scope"])
         self.assertNotIn("gc.scope_ref", steps["finalize"]["metadata"])
 
+        # Running on the abort path only helps if finalize knows it can, and
+        # knows not to fabricate the fields that path legitimately lacks.
+        finalize = node_description(root, steps["finalize"])
+        for fragment in ("ABORTED", "gc.github.review_child_outcome", "backfill"):
+            with self.subTest(step="finalize", fragment=fragment):
+                self.assertIn(fragment, finalize)
+
     def test_github_issue_fix_uses_implementation_plan_artifact_contract(self) -> None:
         root = pathlib.Path(__file__).resolve().parents[1]
         text = effective_formula_text(root, "github-issue-fix")
